From: GPT-6.1-Sol <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6asm: quarantine PCM buffers after uncertain teardown

Complete audit F8 for PCM: track stream, mapping and routing ownership
independently of RUNNING. Use the same checked cleanup on prepare failure,
reprepare and final close. Block reuse after cleanup failure, reserve the
session and synchronously detach its callback before ALSA can disappear.
Transfer the fixed DMA preallocation out of ALSA's freeing path and retain
the device/client/allocation until reboot when DSP quiescence is uncertain.
Never return success for an already allocated mapping. Keep mapping metadata
on timeout, poison indistinguishable command retries, and initialise clients
before publishing them to APR callbacks. Fix the capture unmap base index.

No matching upstream fix found. Quarantine is intentionally conservative:
reclaim on DSP restart needs a separate proven quiescence/lifetime API. It is
bounded by the FE sessions while this service instance remains alive.
Hardware: S16/S24/S32 PCM, repeated prepare/drop/close and capture; inject
format rejection, close/unmap/map/open timeouts. Same FE must return EBUSY
on reopen after quarantine, with no buffer reuse, callback UAF or DSP DMA
fault. Compressed gapless teardown is outside this PCM audit finding.

